A reply cut off at the output-token limit now prints a warning on stderr instead of ending silently. Committed as fba705e7. Build, clippy (-D warnings), fmt --check and the full cargo test all pass.

What changed
• In `src/prompt_retry.rs, classify_stop_reason now sends StopReason::Length to a new StopHandling::OutputLimit (it used to go to Ignore`).
• The warning code is in a new file, src/prompt/output_limit.rs. I put it there because src/prompt.rs and src/prompt_retry.rs are already at their size-gate caps. It has two parts:
  • a pure function, output_limit_note(max_tokens, plain), which builds warning: reply stopped at the output limit (max_tokens = 30); raise --max-tokens or max_tokens in .yoyo.toml. It adds a ⚠ only when output isn't plain, and the caller prints it in yellow.
  • end_turn, which runs where a turn ends and prints the line after any held text has gone to stdout. That one spot covers -p, --print, piped stdin and the REPL. The edit to prompt.rs is two lines.
• **yoagent's behaviour:** I read the source first. yoagent 0.25.2 does not continue or retry on `Length`; `agent_loop.rs:727` treats it as a completed run. So the warning fires only when the turn's last assistant message was cut off. A cut followed by more turns stays silent, and there's a test for that.
• **Exit code stays 0, as planned:** someone who sets a low max_tokens on purpose shouldn't see every run fail. The commit body explains this.
• **Stdout is unchanged:** an end-to-end test against a stub server sends `stop_reason: "max_tokens"` for both `-p` and `--print`. It checks that stdout is byte-for-byte the same as an identical end_turn run, that stderr has the note exactly once, and that the normal run prints nothing about it. I broke the print on purpose, watched that test fail by name, and restored it.
• **The loop's own runs:** nothing in `scripts/` or the workflows uses `-p`. `evolve.sh` pipes the prompt in on stdin and logs with `2>&1 | tee`, so a cut-off session just gains one log line. No harness grep matches it.
• **Docs:** I added a paragraph to docs/src/usage/piped-mode.md and an entry to ARCHITECTURE.md.

Limits
• `--output-format json and stream-json` print no note; they go through a different event loop.
• The number shown is the configured max_tokens. With the older budget-based thinking mode, the Anthropic provider can raise the real request value above it, so the number may be lower than the limit actually used.
• If `max_tokens` isn't set, the note says "the model's default max_tokens", because yoagent doesn't expose the model config's value.
• I changed one existing test, test_classify_stop_reason_normal_stops_untouched: Length no longer belongs in its "ignored" list, so it now asserts Length → OutputLimit instead.
